Textb - an ascii-based Mandelbrot set viewer.This is a hokey little program I adapted from a program which I had adapted from a program in BYTE Magazine a few years back. This outputs the Mandelbrot set to an 80x25 ASCII terminal. To view a portion of the set,run the program, and enter the coordinates of the lowermost-left corner of where you would like to view, and a range which the program will span out. This range is how far the program will travel in the x and y direction, so you are always looking at a square section of the set. A good place to start is as follows:X_Coord: -2.3Y_Coord: -2.0RANGE: 4.0Max. Iter: 32The Max Iter. is the maximum number of iteration on a single point that will be executed before 'bailing out' on that point. Source is included, and may be easily modified to suit any size display or display device type.Enjoy,Russell Hoffmanrh2y+@andrew.cmu.eduCarnegie Mellon University